/* A program with a coercion, a non-terminal T_c and a terminal c_2.  The
   reduction's coercion problem has a rule per terminal, named from the
   terminal, and two copies of each rule, named by suffixes; when those
   were T_<terminal> and <name>_2, the rule for the terminal c_2 and the
   second copy of T_c were both named T_c_2 and the checkers failed on the
   problem.  The program is true: the coercion holds (a copy of the input,
   a list of a, coerced to q0) and the output is a list of c_2. */
%BEGING
Main x -> T_c (coerce q0 (Copy x)).
T_c y -> case y of
  a y' => c_2 (T_c y')
| e => e.
Copy x -> case x of
  a x' => a (Copy x')
| e => e.
%ENDG

%BEGINA
q0 a -> q0.
q0 e -> .
q1 c_2 -> q1.
q1 e -> .
%ENDA

%BEGINT
Main : q0 -> q1.
%ENDT
